The algorithm starts at every element in the first row (since we can start anywhere on the top edge). For each starting point, it explores all valid moves (up/down/left/right), ensuring not to revisit cells already in the current DFS path. When reaching a full-length path (`k` steps), it updates the minimum found so far.

